      { "b", 2, "X and Y boxes move the element. They are not offered for the chat sidebar, the Chat Data Panel or the Character window." },
      { "b", 1, "Nothing changes with the settings window closed, or in combat." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA I3). Chosen for you, change it in the Questions flow (#495): which elements get the menu (every XayaUI element with a settings page), that \"Element options\" opens that page in the window, that X and Y read and write the element's own saved position, and that a restyled Blizzard frame gets \"Element options\" only. Also changed along with it: Rules 0.6.78, Options 0.6.92, Chat 0.6.44, QoL 0.7.51, Bonus Features 0.6.35 and Dev Assist 0.7.61." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-08", title = "Conflict Warnings and Reload on Switch", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.79" },
      { "grp", "Conflict Warnings (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a conflict warning: when another addon that changes the same thing is loaded (ElvUI, EllesmereUI, Prat, SexyMap, BasicMinimap, TipTac, Plater, KuiNameplates, ThreatPlates or idTip), XayaUI says so once at login and on that part's settings page. Nothing is switched off." },
      { "grp", "Reload on Switch" },
      { "b", 1, "Turning Blizzard Reskin, any reskin page, Improved Chat or Nameplates on or off, and /xui chat on||off, /xui reskin on||off and /xui shop, now save and ask for a /reload instead of applying at once. The switch descriptions now say \"Takes effect after a reload\"." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA I2). Also changed along with it: Options 0.6.90, Chat 0.6.43, QoL 0.7.50, Bonus Features 0.6.34, Blizzard Reskin 0.6.23, Nameplates 0.2.3 and Dev Assist 0.7.60." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-08", title = "Settings Migration", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.78" },
      { "grp", "Saved Settings" },
      { "b", 1, "Each addon now keeps its own saved settings: XayaUIReskinDB, XayaUIChatDB, XayaUIBonusDB, XayaUIQoLDB, XayaUIDevAssistDB and XayaUIRulesDB. They are copied once from the old place (CueRulesDB), which is kept. The old place is never written, and nothing is moved or deleted." },
      { "b", 1, "A rules backup, \"Rules before the settings move (<date>)\", appears in Profiles > Backups." },
      { "b", 1, "The counts are compared after the copy. If they do not match, that addon keeps reading the old place, and a warning, XUI-W006, is shown once." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (walkthrough H16). Removing the old keys is not built (phase P6). Also changed along with it: Rules 0.6.77, Rules Options 0.6.78, QoL 0.7.49, Bonus Features 0.6.33, Chat 0.6.42, Blizzard Reskin 0.6.22 and Dev Assist 0.7.59." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-08", title = "Rules Options Folder", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.77" },
      { "grp", "Install (read this first)" },
      { "b", 1, "Copy the second new folder, XayaUI_Rules_Options, into AddOns as well, next to XayaUI_Rules. The AddOns list gains \"XayaUI Rules Options\". It loads only when the rule editor opens." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (walkthrough H15). You asked to build everything without waiting for your in-game test, so the Accept for the earlier code move (H14) no longer blocks the next phase." },
      { "h3", "Rules Options 0.6.77" },
      { "grp", "XayaUI Rules Options (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added XayaUI Rules Options, a load-on-demand addon that holds the rule editor." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-07", title = "XayaUI Rules Is Its Own Addon", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.76" },
      { "grp", "Install (read this first)" },
      { "b", 1, "Copy the new XayaUI_Rules folder into AddOns AND replace the whole XayaUI folder (22 files left it, and GameMenu.lua is now GameMenuButton.lua). Without XayaUI_Rules no rules run." },
      { "grp", "XayaUI Platform" },
      { "b", 1, "The XayaUI folder is now titled \"XayaUI Platform\" in the AddOns list. It keeps your saved data (CueRulesDB), and nothing in it moves. Rules strings you exported before still import." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game; it needs your in-game Accept (walkthroughs \"code-move\", \"code-move-off\" and \"code-move-on\", QA H14) before phase P5 of the platform split. Replacing the whole XayaUI folder keeps it clean: the game loads only the files the addon's list names, so leftover files are unused." },
      { "h3", "Rules 0.6.76" },
      { "grp", "XayaUI Rules (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added XayaUI Rules, a new addon that holds the rule engine, triggers, cues and displays, combat aura tracking, and rule sharing and the rules Recycle Bin, moved out of the XayaUI folder. You named it (\"Call it Rules\")." },
      { "b", 1, "XayaUI Rules can be switched off in the AddOns list: the rule commands answer that it is off, the Rules tabs and the rules part of Profiles are hidden, and Import shows the rules part as \"needs XayaUI Rules\"." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.84" },
      { "grp", "Internal" },
      { "b", 1, "Internal: every addon now reads its settings through ns.Settings(module), and the rule editor and rules tree moved out of Options.lua into their own files (QoL 0.7.48, Bonus Features 0.6.32 and Dev Assist 0.7.57 were updated along with them). Nothing visible." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA H12 and H13)." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-07", title = "Platform Services", blocks = {
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.80" },
      { "grp", "Profiles" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a Nameplates part to Profiles: Export and Import carry your target color." },
      { "b", 1, "Import now skips a part whose addon is not loaded and shows \"needs <addon>\" for it, instead of dropping it silently." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA H11; walkthroughs \"platform-services\" and \"platform-services-reload\" in /xui dev qa). The rest of this landing is groundwork with nothing visible: profile parts and Recycle Bin kinds that each addon registers itself, theme scopes, and aura and tooltip services for Bonus Features." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-07", title = "What Changed Overnight", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.73" },
      { "grp", "Commands" },
      { "b", 1, "/xui help now lists \"/xui data (Data Panels)\" in place of \"custom data panels and bars\"." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: The hovers of the minimap button, the mover's group tabs and the chat's privacy, history and collapse buttons now share one helper; they read and look as before (QA B279). Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Engine and Performance" },
      { "b", 1, "Rule and snapshot log lines are now built only while something reads them (the console window, the debug strip, or the record)." },
      { "b", 1, "Rules that are not loaded are no longer read during engine steps, except for a buff a display on that rule needs." },
      { "b", 1, "Removed closures that the engine created for every rule read, and most errors from other addons no longer cost a call-stack read." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Measured on stand-ins only, not in game." },
      { "b", 1, "An aura the game hides now reads \"hidden by the game right now ...\", and the rule status says whether the game's container still draws the display." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.72" },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "Added new top tabs: Rules, QoL, Bonus Features, Blizzard Reskin, Profiles and Settings. The toolbar is gone: \"+ New Rule\" is at the left of the Rules row, and the Settings cog is now the Settings tab. The Blizzard UI Reskin tab is now called Blizzard Reskin everywhere a player reads it, including the Overview switch \"Enable Blizzard Reskin\" and chat messages." },
      { "b", 1, "Added Profiles, with sub-tabs Import, Export and Recycle Bin. Export has one tick box per component (Rules and groups, Themes, Settings, QoL, Bonus Features, Blizzard Reskin); anything beyond Rules and groups makes a profile string. Import lists only what the string holds, each with a tick box." },
      { "b", 1, "Hover texts are now at most two sentences." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game. Chosen for you, change it in the Questions flow: which settings each Profiles component holds, and what is never exported (Notepad, Shopping List, Recycle Bin, backups, drafts, calculator history, other players' names). Questions UI-25-newrule, UI-27-components, UI-27-personal, UI-27-merge, UI-27-backups, UI-27-eui and UI-24-label-scope." },
      { "b", 1, "The settings window now responds faster to clicks when there are many rules: only the rule on screen is built, and a click no longer rebuilds every rule's editor." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Offline measurement only (313 rules, a click from 1,715 ms to about 100-200 ms of Lua). The window's narrowest width now follows only the dropdowns of rules you have opened (Q-PERF-8)." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-07", title = "Bar Cues", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.58" },
      { "grp", "Bar Cues (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a Bar cue: a progress bar that tracks an aura's time left, a spell's cooldown or recharge, stacks, or charges. Make one with New Rule > Progress Bar, or Add a cue > Bar on any rule." },
      { "b", 2, "A new bar is 220 x 22 with a black 20% background, a 1 px border and a flat texture, draining from right to left, with the spell's icon on the left, its name inside the bar, the time on the right and a spark on the moving edge." },
      { "b", 2, "Tracks: Automatic (the aura, else the spell's cooldown), Aura time left, Spell cooldown / recharge, Stacks, or Charges. Maximum 0 uses the game's own maximum; if the game gives none, the bar stays empty." },
      { "b", 2, "Drain toward the left, right, bottom or top, or fill up instead. The icon can sit left, right or be hidden. The spark can be turned off and recolored." },
      { "b", 2, "Automatic color follows the type the spell's tooltip names (a school written as \"<school> damage\", or a dispel type), then the aura's dispel type, then blue." },
      { "b", 2, "Color style per bar: Blizzard default, Neon, Pastel, Muted / Dark, or Custom with a color for each of 12 types. A group's Display tab has \"Every bar: color style\", with \"Force on every bar in this group\" to override each bar's own choice." },
      { "b", 2, "Bar textures: Flat, Blizzard, Raid frame, the game's own power-bar art, any texture shared through LibSharedMedia, or your own file." },
      { "b", 2, "In combat, aura-time and stacks bars are drawn by the game's own aura buttons and keep moving while the game hides aura numbers. Cooldown bars are driven by the game from the cooldown's duration." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA B200-B210). The combat drawing is built from Blizzard's 12.1.5 source and tested on a stand-in only." },
      { "grp", "Engine" },
      { "b", 1, "Cooldown and aura cues now react one frame after the change instead of up to 58 ms later, and only the rules that read what changed are re-checked." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Measured on a stand-in only (worst delay 58 ms to 8.3 ms, about 12% fewer rule checks), not in game (QA B199, B211, B212)." },
      { "b", 1, "Reworked how closing the settings window ends the previews and unlocks it started (a structure fix to the earlier change)." },
      { "b", 1, "Once you have played a spec, its Auto-populate list shows that spec's Cooldown Manager auras and debuffs." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.59" },
      { "grp", "Bar Cues (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a Bar Options box on each Bar cue, and \"Every bar: color style\" on a group's Display tab." },
      { "b", 1, "Smart Categories > Progress Bars now lists rules that have a Bar cue." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-06", title = "Debug Report, Group Page and Auto-populate Buttons", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.57" },
      { "grp", "Debug Report (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added error codes and a debug report. XayaUI now records only errors and warnings, each with a code (XUI-E...), and only when they happen, so it costs nothing otherwise." },
      { "b", 2, "/xui report opens a readable summary you can screenshot, with a Copy string you can send." },
      { "b", 2, "The detailed record kinds (rule snapshots, aura answers and so on) now live in Dev Assist." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Developer Tools" },
      { "b", 1, "The developer diagnostics now exist only while Dev Assist is installed and enabled: /xui debug probe, timing, model, tracker, mods, groups, icons, media, seed, map, gamemenu, chatprobe, widthprobe, perf ui, debuffs and loc, /xuitt probe, lines and aura, /xui chat wrap, indent and whispers, /xuiskin pad and alpha, and /xuiengine auto, on, off and reset." },
      { "b", 1, "Players keep /xui debug perf, /xui debug loader, /xui status, /xui auras, /xuiskin (turns the window skin off), and /xuiengine full and refresh." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Group Page" },
      { "b", 1, "Added the tabs Group, Display, Load and Config to a group's page, with Group first." },
      { "b", 2, "Config holds the name, an Enabled switch, the group type, Sound Channel Override, new rule / nested group / delete, and \"Made by: <character>\"." },
      { "b", 1, "Added a group Size (Auto or Set, with optional Clip), and Border and Background tick boxes with color, texture and padding." },
      { "b", 1, "Added \"Anchored to: The parent group / The screen\" for nested groups." },
      { "b", 1, "Added Align & Arrange to static groups (Align left / center / right, Distribute, Space with a gap). The choice is saved: a display you drag, nudge, add or resize goes back into line." },
      { "b", 1, "Added \"Scale items to fit the box\" for static groups with a Set size. Making the box smaller than its items asks \"Scale the items to fit?\" once." },
      { "b", 1, "Added Limit (show at most N) and Align (Top / Center / Bottom, or Left / Center / Right) to dynamic groups." },
      { "b", 1, "A rule's display position now reads \"Anchor point\", then \"Anchored to:\", then \"To <target>'s point\", and changing either no longer moves the display." },
      { "b", 1, "Fixed an issue where \"Outside\" with a corner anchor acted as \"Inside\"." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Mover View" },
      { "b", 1, "Added arrow-key nudging of the display or group you last clicked: 1 pixel, 10 with Shift. Not in combat." },
      { "b", 1, "Added a small lock on each group's name tab that locks the group for now so you can reach what is under it. Nothing is saved." },
      { "b", 1, "Leaving the mover view after moving something now asks Save moves or Cancel moves; Cancel puts everything back. Moves left by a /reload or logout without Save are offered back at login." },
      { "b", 1, "The same prompt now shows when the settings window closes after it unlocked the displays and something moved." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game. A game crash cannot keep unsaved moves: the game writes saved data only at logout or /reload." },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "Closing the settings window now ends every preview, sidebar movement unlock, group unlock, preview pause and window-made unlock." },
      { "b", 1, "Fixed an issue where previews stayed on screen after the settings window closed." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Rules" },
      { "b", 1, "Added the trigger choice Player State \"Dead, not released\"." },
      { "b", 1, "A rule that is switched off now costs nothing: no engine work and no display frame. Preview still works, and the rule is not shown in the unlock view." },
      { "b", 1, "A talent in a rule's Load tab now clicks through Known (green), Not known (red) and Not set." },
      { "b", 1, "New Sound cues now start on the SFX channel." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.57" },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "Added even, thicker top tabs, no pane borders (a divider line instead), nested rows indented under their parent, and greyed-out settings and names under a feature that is switched off." },
      { "b", 1, "The Blizzard UI Reskin tab now starts with an Overview row. \"Enable Blizzard UI Reskin\" is a tick box on that page, with a Reload / Later prompt, and the reskins' own pages show once it is on. This replaces the \"All reskins\" tick box on the tab." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game." },
      { "grp", "Auto-populate" },
      { "b", 1, "Replaced the Auto-populate buttons with four per spec (and four for the class): Generate All Rules, Generate CD Tracking Rules, Generate Aura Tracking Rules and Generate Target Debuff Tracking Rules. A button filters the table below it, and nothing is made until you press Populate." },
      { "b", 2, "Added a Select all tick box above the table that ticks only the rows shown." },
      { "b", 2, "For a spec you are not in, the Aura and Target Debuff buttons list nothing and tell you to switch to that spec first." },
      { "b", 1, "Added a titled auto-populate table: rows grouped under Spell CD, Aura and Debuff, a Spec column when listing every spec, and each spell's icon." },
      { "b", 2, "Added a Cue set-up column: Speech has a \"Customize\" box, and Sound and pictures have a picker you must choose from." },
      { "b", 2, "A row that could not be made stays in the table with an error popup; made rows leave it." },
      { "b", 2, "On-screen cues are placed in rows of 3 centered on the screen." },
      { "b", 2, "Added a \"Hide / Show already generated rules\" switch." },
      { "b", 1, "The Cooldown Manager warning now reads \"Blizzard's Cooldown Manager does not offer in-combat tracking for this aura for your current spec. Rule might not work reliably.\" where the game offers no tracking." },
      { "b", 1, "Combat Tracking Setup moved from the Debugging page to Settings > UI Options > Rule Creation." },
      { "b", 1, "Added the sidebar look: XayaUI's own eye and headphone icons, a flat padlock and a gold move arrow, \"Delete (N)\", \"Move (N)\" and \"Deselect (N)\", and \"Link N Selected (move together)\" in the right-click menu." },
      { "b", 1, "Pressing a rule row and moving the mouse now starts a drag, with a line or highlighted group showing where it lands." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game. The button width is an estimate, and the aura and debuff lists rely on an inference about the Cooldown Manager's fields." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.56" },
      { "grp", "Patch Notes and Info (new)" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a pane that opens when you click the version text in the settings window's bottom-left corner. It floats above the settings window, can be dragged by its title bar and reopens where you left it." },
      { "b", 2, "Patch Notes: What's New (new features only, newest first, per addon) and one entry per update." },
      { "b", 2, "Info: Version info, Readme, Help (FAQ) and Credits + Acknowledgments." },
      { "b", 1, "Added a ? button to the settings window's title bar, beside collapse and X. It opens Info > Help (FAQ); the pane has the same button." },
      { "b", 1, "Addon Info and Settings > Acknowledgments moved into the pane." },
      { "b", 1, "Esc closes the pane first, then the settings window." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Not yet tested in game (QA B197). In combat the game does not let addons hold Esc back, so one Esc closes both windows there." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-06", title = "Character Pane, Shopping List and All Reskins", blocks = {
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.50" },
      { "grp", "Dynamic Groups" },
      { "b", 1, "The group's Sort choices are now listed Default, Expiration, Name, Important, Manual. Manual is still the default." },
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.50" },
      { "grp", "Console" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a command line to the console (`/xui console`). It takes any XayaUI command, with or without `/xui`; Up and Down bring back earlier commands." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Up / Down recall, and `/save` and `/reload` from the console, are not yet tested in game." },
      { "b", 1, "All diagnostic commands now live under `/xui debug` (type `/xui debug` for the list) and print in the console. `/xui debug window` is renamed `/xui debug loader`." },
      { "b", 1, "`/xui help` is now shorter: only the commands a player uses." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.43" },
      { "grp", "Cooldown Manager Warnings" },
      { "b", 1, "Added a warning when a rule follows an aura or target debuff that the game hides in combat and Blizzard's Cooldown Manager is not tracking. The rule's Display and Cues tabs say where to add it (with XayaUI 0.6.48)." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: XayaUI cannot add it to the Cooldown Manager for you: Blizzard keeps that window closed to addons." },
    } },
    { date = "2026-11-05", title = "Blizzard UI Reskin tab and Switched-off Features", blocks = {
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.49" },
      { "grp", "Debugging" },
      { "b", 1, "Added `/xui debug map`, a report command for the full-screen world map problem. It prints the map's state so the cause can be found; it does not fix the problem yet." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.41" },
      { "grp", "Class/Spec Rule Creator" },
      { "b", 1, "Added Choose which rules to make: tick only the cooldowns and target debuffs you want, pick each one's main cue, then Make the ticked rules. Your choices are kept per spec." },
      { "dev", 2, "Developers' notes: Two different changes on main carry the label Options 0.6.41. They are listed as they are; history is not renumbered." },
      { "b", 1, "Switched-off features now cost nothing: a feature you turn off no longer runs timers, listens to events or keeps frames (with Chat 0.6.14, XayaUI 0.6.47, Blizzard Reskin 0.6.2 and Bonus Features 0.6.12)." },
      { "h3", "XayaUI 0.6.46" },
      { "grp", "Themes" },
      { "b", 1, "Added each Gradient Cursor Trail gradient as a UI theme in Settings > Theme (\"Cursor trail: <name>\"). The trail can follow your UI theme, and the Cursor Highlight can use your theme's accent color (with Quality of Life 0.7.17)." },
      { "b", 1, "`/xui help` is now one command per line, with the command in your theme's accent color." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.40" },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "In QoL and Bonus Features, each feature's on / off is now a tick box beside its name in the left pane." },
      { "b", 1, "Notepad and Calculator are now grouped under a new Utilities entry in Bonus Features." },
      { "b", 1, "Scan all talents now lives under Settings > UI Options > Rule Creation (`/xui talents` still works)." },
      { "h3", "Options 0.6.39" },
      { "grp", "Settings Window" },
      { "b", 1, "The version text at the bottom of the settings window now replaces the Addon Info button and uses your theme colors." },
      { "b", 1, "Console switches in settings no longer pause while the whole window rebuilds (with XayaUI 0.6.45)." },
    } },
  },
  readme = {
    { "h2", "What XayaUI is" },
    { "p", "XayaUI is a group of addons. Each one is its own entry in the game's AddOns list (under XayaUI), so you can switch any of them off; the game needs a /reload after a change there." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI** holds the rules (cooldown, aura and other triggers), cues, conditions and actions, combat aura tracking, sharing and backups, themes, the console, the minimap button and the Esc-menu button. Every other XayaUI addon needs it." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Options** is the settings window. It loads the first time you open it, so it costs nothing until then." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Chat** holds the Chat Panel, the Chat Data Panel, message filters and sounds, history and the privacy cover." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI QoL** holds the cursor highlight and trail, the Character Reskin, the Shopping List and Release Guard." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Bonus Features** holds the Stat Calculator (Bonus Features > Stat Calculator, or `/xui stats`)." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Blizzard Reskin** puts XayaUI's look on Blizzard's frames without changing what they do (today: the Esc menu)." },
    { "b", 1, "**XayaUI Media** is a support folder for your own pictures and sounds." },
    { "p", "A feature you switch off costs nothing: it runs no timers, listens to no events and keeps no frames. Your settings are kept either way." },
    { "h2", "Getting started" },
    { "b", 1, "Open the settings window with `/xui`, the XayaUI minimap button, or the XayaUI button in the Esc menu." },
    { "b", 1, "**Rules** is where you make and edit rules. A rule watches something (a trigger), and when it is true it plays cues (a sound, speech, an icon), checks conditions and runs actions." },
    { "b", 1, "**QoL**, **Bonus Features** and **Blizzard UI Reskin** each list their features in the left pane. The tick box beside a name turns that feature on or off; hover it for what it does." },
    { "b", 1, "**Settings** (the toolbar button) holds UI Options (Display, Rule Creation, Theme), the Minimap Button and Debugging." },
    { "b", 1, "Click the version text in the settings window's bottom-left corner for this window: Patch Notes and Info. The **?** in the title bar opens Help." },
    { "h2", "Features at a glance" },
    { "b", 1, "**Auto-Generate Rules.** Builds a first batch of rules for your spec: one skeleton rule per cooldown, and you choose which to make. Rules > Auto-Generate Rules." },
    { "b", 1, "**Chat Panel.** Reskins Blizzard's chat in place, with a Chat Data Panel, filters, history, per-tab sounds and a privacy cover. Blizzard UI Reskin > Chat Panel, or `/xui chat settings`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Character Reskin.** Blizzard's character window in XayaUI's look: item levels colored by upgrade track, enchant and gem lines, a wider and taller window, and the full stat list. Blizzard UI Reskin > Character Pane, or `/xui reskin`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Stat Calculator.** A panel beside the character window with your stats, gear and ability scaling. Bonus Features > Stat Calculator, or `/xui stats`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Shopping List.** What your gear is missing and what your tracked recipes need. Blizzard UI Reskin > Shopping List, or `/xui shop`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Release Guard.** Covers the Release Spirit button when you die so a misclick does not release you. QoL > Release Guard." },
    { "b", 1, "**Cursor Highlight and Trail.** A colored shape at the cursor and a trail of gradient dots, to find the mouse easily. Both off by default. QoL > Cursor, or `/xui cursor`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Enhanced Tooltips.** ID lines for spells, items, auras and NPCs (more if you turn them on), and Aura ID lines for the effects an item or spell describes. Bonus Features > Enhanced Tooltips." },
    { "b", 1, "**Notepad and Calculator.** Bonus Features > Utilities, or `/notes` and `/calc`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Data Panels.** Your own panels and bars of live information. `/xui data`." },
    { "b", 1, "**Themes.** Colors and fonts for every XayaUI window. Settings > UI Options > Theme." },
    { "b", 1, "**Debugging.** Advanced Debugging records what is needed to find a problem. Settings > Debugging." },
    { "h2", "Slash commands" },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui` opens or closes the settings window (`/xayaui` works too)." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui help` lists every command you can use." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui console` opens the XayaUI console: its messages, and a line to type commands in." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui status` prints every rule's answer right now, and why." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui auras` prints aura IDs, and whether XayaUI can follow them in combat." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui unlock` lets you drag displays and groups; type it again to lock." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui bug` makes a bug report." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui debug` lists the diagnostic commands." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui chat`, `/xui panel`, `/xui privacy` for the Chat Panel, the Chat Data Panel and the privacy cover." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui reskin`, `/xui stats`, `/xui shop`, `/xui cursor` for the QoL features." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui notes`, `/xui calc`, `/xui data` for the Bonus Features." },
    { "p", "The full manual is docs/USER-GUIDE.md in the XayaUI source code (Info > Version info has the link)." },
  },
  faq = {
    { "h2", "Rules not firing" },
    { "h3", "My rule never fires." },
    { "p", "Usually one of its inputs is unknown (shown in yellow), or the rule does not load. Type `/xui status` (or `/xui debug status`) for every rule's answer right now and why, read the Right now lines, and check the dots on the condition rows." },
    { "h3", "The rule fires but I get no sound or display." },
    { "p", "The rule has conditions, but no cue is listed in any enabled condition's THEN row. Open the rule's Conditions tab and add the cue there." },
    { "h3", "The rule does not load at all." },
    { "p", "Its group is set to Never, a group's class, spec, role or instance setting keeps it out, or a talent requirement is not met. The Load tab's banner says \"Overridden by group...\" when a group is the reason." },
    { "h3", "It works out of combat but not in combat." },
    { "p", "The value it reads is secret in combat, so the answer becomes unknown. The Right now line shows it; see \"What the game won't allow\" below." },
    { "h3", "It fires one or two seconds early." },
    { "p", "Spell Usable ignores the cooldown. Use \"Usable AND off cooldown\" instead." },
    { "h3", "It says \"not set: cooldown state\" or \"a trigger (none added yet)\"." },
    { "p", "A section is in use but its State dropdown is blank, or there is no trigger and both states are blank. Fix it on the Trigger tab." },
    { "h2", "Auras and the Cooldown Manager" },
    { "h3", "How do I find an aura's ID?" },
    { "p", "Out of combat, with the aura on you (a training dummy works), type `/xui auras` for your buffs or `/xui auras debuffs`. `/xui auras <spell ID or name>` prints the same facts for one spell and works anywhere, in combat too." },
    { "h3", "Can XayaUI follow this aura in combat?" },
    { "p", "The same command answers it:" },
    { "b", 1, "**Readable in combat:** \"yes (never secret)\" for the few auras the game always lets addons read; otherwise \"no (secret in combat, encounters, Mythic+ and PvP)\"." },
    { "b", 1, "**Cooldown Manager:** \"on and shown\" means XayaUI sees the aura in combat. \"Offered ... but not switched on\" means your spec's Blizzard Cooldown Manager has it: turn it on there (Tracked Buffs or Tracked Bars)." },
    { "h3", "Why can't XayaUI add the aura to the Cooldown Manager for me?" },
    { "p", "Blizzard keeps that window closed to addons. When a rule needs it, the rule's Display and Cues tabs say where to add it." },
    { "h2", "What the game won't allow" },
    { "h3", "Why is there no trigger for health, mana, rage or the combat log?" },
    { "p", "In Midnight (12.x) primary resources, combat log events, health, other units' casts and creature identity are not available to addons, so those triggers were not ported. Enemy aura reads are unavailable too." },
    { "h3", "Why do some answers go unknown in combat?" },
    { "p", "Buff and debuff reads in restricted content may be secret. The Cooldown Manager icon is the fallback, and only for spells tracked there. Target Debuff in combat relies on the spell being tracked in the Cooldown Manager buff viewer." },
    { "h3", "Why does my glow action do nothing?" },
    { "p", "A glow needs the LibCustomGlow library, which XayaUI does not ship. Enable ElvUI, BigWigs or another addon that ships it." },
    { "h3", "Why don't my custom cues play?" },
    { "p", "Custom cues can be made but do not yet play, show or run anything." },
    { "h3", "Why can't my chat action send to other players?" },
    { "p", "The game restricts chat actions to other players in several kinds of content, and combat numbers cannot be put in chat." },
    { "h2", "Commands and reporting" },
    { "h3", "Where are the commands?" },
    { "p", "`/xui help` lists the commands you use. The diagnostic ones are under `/xui debug`; `/xui debug` alone lists them. Any `/xui debug` command opens the XayaUI console and prints there." },
    { "h3", "Where are XayaUI's messages?" },
    { "p", "In the main chat window, the XayaUI console window (`/xui console`), or both: choose under Settings > Debugging, \"XayaUI's messages\"." },
    { "h3", "How do I report a problem?" },
    { "b", 1, "Turn on **Advanced Debugging** (Settings > Debugging; recommended). It records what is needed to find a problem, so you do not have to remember a command." },
    { "b", 1, "Type `/reload` (or log out): the game writes its files only then." },
    { "b", 1, "Send `XayaUI.lua` from `World of Warcraft\\_retail_\\WTF\\Account\\<your account folder>\\SavedVariables\\`. Settings > Debugging shows the exact path and what to send." },
    { "b", 1, "`/xui bug` makes a bug report." },
  },
}
